        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After the financial account is identified, always display the selected account information in a natural-language sentence, for example: I see that your selected account has the following details: FinancialAccountName: {FinancialAccountName}, FinancialAccountNumber: {FinancialAccountNumber}, Type: {FinancialAccountType} strictly in a single line separated by commas , retrieve and display all financial account balances associated with the selected financial account. Use the GetBalancesFromFinancialAccounts action to retrieve the balance details for the selected financial account, including available balance, total balance, and any other relevant details. IMPORTANT - Pass financialAccountId from the selected Financial Account to GetBalancesFromFinancialAccounts action input. Display all balances in a numbered list format; each item of list should have details like balance type and amount. Always make sure the currency symbol should be before or after the balance amount according to the convention followed for currency. If no balances are found for the selected financial account, display “There are no balances for your selected financial account.” Then, ask if the customer wants to check the balance for another financial account and display all available customer financial accounts. Do not display balance from previous conversations.</description>
